## 5. Traps — read before touching anything

### 5.1 A clean compiler run proves nothing

`scripts/compile-corpus-index.py` (1,412 lines, **zero arguments**) has seven silent-skip sites. Malformed input is indistinguishable from absent input:

- 8 of 27 entries absent from `TEXT_DIRS` → invisible, no warning (collection iterates the registry, not the filesystem)
- 4 of 11 `tension-edges.json` files yield **zero** edges silently, dropping 55 records (`:1128-1129`)
- `parse_ontology_md` returns `[]` rather than erroring
- No `--check`, no non-zero exit, no self-check against manifest counts

**Never verify a repair by "the compiler ran clean."** Phase 1 exists to fix this and must land before Phase 4.

### 5.2 The output is not byte-reproducible

`canonicalTerms` sorts on `(-len, lower())`; 101 case-duplicate pairs tie and flip per run under Python's randomized set iteration. Every recompile dirties a git-tracked file with meaningless reordering.

### 5.3 The compiler reads no JSON ontologies

`ontology.json` appears **nowhere** in its 1,412 lines. It dispatches on `ontology_format` with two handlers (`header` ×17, `table` ×2). A third (`json`) is an established pattern, ~1 day, +102 concepts.

### 5.4 Renaming an entry directory silently drops it

`TEXT_DIRS` is keyed by directory name. Five entry paths are also hardcoded in `scripts/normalize-edges.py:37-41`. `deriveAuthor` parses the display label by splitting on `' - '` and the result becomes a ChromaDB `author_raw` filter — renaming breaks author-scoped retrieval.

### 5.5 `doc_id` is path-derived

`doc_id = sha256(f'{path_rel}:{sha256_file}')[:16]`, chunk ids `{doc_id}:{idx:05d}` (`run_ingest_phase2.py:220-222, :659, :699`). **Relocating any document mints a new namespace with no dedup against old chunks.** In Phase 2, purge before moving.

### 5.6 The index is being ingested right now

772 of 1,182 manifest records are under `index/`; 25 chunks are live in ChromaDB with `collection="index"`. No walker excludes `index` — `SKIP_DIRS = {".extracted_media", "__pycache__", "node_modules", ".git", ".ingest_cache"}`.

### 5.7 Stale facts in memory files — correct these

| Recorded | Actual |
|---|---|
| "ChromaDB collections metaphysics/new_media/rhetorical_ontology" | **One collection, `knowledge_chunks`.** Those are values of a per-chunk metadata field, filtered by `where` |
| "QuotationFidelityValidator (70%+)" | Threshold is **0.90** (`quotation-fidelity-stage.ts:60-61`) |
| "QualityGauntlet (7 stages)" | **10 default stages** (`quality-gauntlet.ts:574-589`); comments still say 7 |
| "Secondary clusters NOT registered, by design" | **Reversed in practice** — Boredom Secondary (68) and VR Pedagogy (60) are the two largest contributors |
| "corpus/index FIRST, ChromaDB fallback" | **A human workflow rule only.** Zero code implements it; live order is inverted |

### 5.8 Service state

Local `:8000` (embedder), `:8001` (Chroma), `:8002` (vLLM) were **down** at audit time with stale pid files (`.run/chroma.pid` 5972, `.run/embedder.pid` 6008, `.run/marker.pid` 6555). `wraith-infer` on WRAITH `:8100` (GPU 1) was live serving gte-Qwen2-1.5B + `bge-reranker-v2-m3`. **Re-check before relying on any of them** — start with `/god-launch`.

### 5.9 Retrieval changes here are not reliably improvements

Recorded eval: raw 1536 gte-Qwen2 was a **regression** vs 768 fastembed (MRR 0.285 vs 0.493); the cross-encoder reranker was the win (768+rerank MRR 0.547). **A/B any retrieval change before default-on**, especially index-first ordering in Phase 5C.

